WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.390
Hello, everyone. You may have noticed,

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.390
I live in England and
it's the middle of winter.

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:09.350
It's freezing.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.890
So I'm gonna warm myself up today

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.073
with a lot of cups of tea, delicious.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:14.873
Nah , it's not true.

00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:15.730
What I'm doing is,

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.460
you may have noticed that all
the descriptions of the videos

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.000
I always write filmed at,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.720
a thousand FPS or something,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.090
and the FPS stands for frames per second.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.380
Basically our high speed camera,

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.320
the higher the frame rate,

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.340
the slower the motion.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.123
Is how many pictures it's
taking in one second basically.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.610
So I'm gonna smash these mugs

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.570
at 500, a thousand, 2,500
and 5000 frames a second.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.720
They're all pretty common
frame rates to my channel

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.350
if you've seen previous videos.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.220
But there's one frame
rate I'm going to do today

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.598
that I've never done
before on the channel.

00:00:47.598 --> 00:00:49.410
10,000 frames a second.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.940
It has to be a reduced resolution,

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.170
but we'll see how it turns out.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.763
I'm pretty sure it's
gonna be horribly slow.

00:00:55.731 --> 00:00:56.564
But we'll see.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.930
All right, this is where we
do quite a lot of our filming,

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:04.980
but as you can see, it's winter.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.340
So the sun is so low.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.563
Even on a sunny day,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.070
the sun never actually
touches the ground here.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.520
So I'm gonna have to
do this somewhere else.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:02.750
Now the reason I have to
do this in the sunlight,

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.563
is because as you'll notice,

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.370
as the frame rate goes up,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.400
the light goes down.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.550
Gets darker and darker
as you shoot faster.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:15.453
And at 10,000 frames,

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.000
it's pretty freaking dark.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.250
All right, well, now we have
a good speed comparison.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:06.570
Thanks to these poor innocent mugs.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.610
Before I turn this off, I'm gonna say,

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:11.587
go and watch "Sherlock
Holmes" the second movie,

00:04:11.587 --> 00:04:13.180
"A Game of Shadows"

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.440
because I worked on it

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.320
and there's a ton of slow motion in it.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.830
Shot with this exact camera

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.020
that I use for the slow-mo guys.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.050
So watch the movie,

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.850
let me know what you think of the slow-mo.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:26.560
I honestly think is probably,

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.610
one of the most mental
action scenes I've ever seen.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.610
So let me know what you think.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:32.443
See you later.

